<time datetime="2023-08-14">August 14, 2023</time>
<article id="URL" class="WebBits">
    <h2>TRY: Review data storage</h2>
    <div class="columns">
        <p class="col-d-9 col-dl-6">
            Data storage is elemental to a website's operation. Viewing a web
            page doesn't involve disk storage, and the webpage's source code
            isn't saved. Instead, it is retrieved from a web server through web
            requests on each iteration. Go to
            <span data-rwb-type="link"><a href="markup.html" title="Markup&lt;/RWB&gt;">&lt;Markup&gt;</a></span>
            for viewing source code.
        </p>
        <p class="col-d-9 col-dl-6">
            Data from one web page is sometimes needed for concurrent web pages.
            While a server <em>can</em> save the needed data, doing so is
            inefficient and adds unnecessary upkeep and maintenance of the
            server. The browser offers the developer 'localStorage' for this use
            case.
        </p>
        <aside class="exampleBlue">
            Go to
            <span data-rwb-type="link">
                <a href="guides/devtools/applicationtab.html"
                   title="GUIDE: Dev Application&lt;/RWB&gt;">&lt;GUIDE: Dev Application&gt;</a>
            </span>
            for a bit on local storage.
        </aside>
        <p class="col-d-9 col-dl-12">
            Browser's local storage is domain-based. That means dev tools will
            report data for each domain holding data. On the home page,
            <a href="https://randomwebbits.com" title="&lt;Random Web Bits&gt; | Home">https://randomwebbits.com</a>,
            the
            To-Do list stores each to-do in a local storage key called
            `ToDos`. Also, the Dictionary Term component stores words cached as
            JSON objects to save all the previously searched words.
        </p>
    </div>
</article>
<div class="Top-Link"><a class="Top" href="/pages/datastorage#top">Top</a></div>
@section Scripts {
    <script type="text/javascript">
        document.querySelector("body").classList.add("WebBits-width");
    </script>
}